cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "passyield: the nominal-versus-realised data-yield shortfall of a ground-station contact, as a distribution"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-19"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmAcharya-avtr/passyield"
abstract: >-
  passyield measures the data-yield shortfall of a scheduled ground-station
  contact against the nominal duration and rate the scheduler booked, and
  decomposes it into geometry, acquisition, re-synchronisation and idle time
  with the closing residual of the identity reported as a number. The headline
  output is a distribution with its quantiles, not a point shortfall, because
  a contact schedule can only be written against a random variable by booking
  a quantile of it. Pass geometry comes from an SGP4 propagation of a published
  verification element set; the analytic baseline is a mass-preserving
  pushforward and a compound-Poisson convolution over the pass geometry,
  cross-checked against a direct Monte Carlo of the same laws and bracketed by
  a bound derived from the pass duration and the rate ceiling alone. A learned
  per-pass predictor with an uncertainty output is scored on held-out stations
  and held-out time separately. Research-grade; not flight-qualified, not
  certified and not approved for operational aerospace use.
keywords:
  - ground station
  - contact scheduling
  - data yield
  - SGP4
  - link budget
  - compound Poisson
  - convolution
  - bootstrap
  - CRPS
  - calibration
